# Adversarial Verification Harness

**Self-test:** Can I name the exact files I'll modify? If NO → plan first.

| Complexity | Approach |
|---|---|
| Simple (named files, no architectural impact) | Just do it. |
| Non-trivial (vague, 3+ files, architectural) | **`/planner` FIRST.** |

- No `state.json` → `/planner`. Has `state.json` → resume next pending task.
- Building → need `.harness/contract.json` before impl (hooks deny ungated writes).
- Do not self-certify → `/evaluator` PASS before `verified: true`.
- Multi-file work → TodoWrite + breadcrumb in `.harness/breadcrumbs.jsonl` (hook-enforced).
- User says `skip harness` → opt out.

Roles: `/planner` (vision, max 5 tasks, no code) · Builder (contract + impl) · `/evaluator` (negotiate + verify; `.harness/` only).

Procedure: skill `adversarial-harness`. Design: `docs/HARNESS_ESSENCE.md`.
